SUMMARY:🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂
 🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂\n\n### A Hidden Ravine\, Easy Wa
 lking & Great Conversation\n\nSometimes the best parts of Toronto are the 
 ones most people drive right past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed fall walk alon
 g the **Gus Harris Trail**\, a quiet ravine trail that follows **Taylor-Ma
 ssey Creek** through Scarborough and East York.\n\nThis isn't a challengin
 g hike. It's an easy\, mostly flat walk through one of Toronto's quieter g
 reen spaces\, with plenty of time to enjoy the changing leaves\, get some 
 fresh air\, and meet other people along the way.\n\nWe'll follow the creek
 \, walk beneath the trees\, and take our time enjoying the fall scenery.\n
 The goal isn't to race to the end of the trail. **It's to get outside\, ha
 ve some good conversations\, and enjoy the company.**\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:**
  Taylor-Massey Creek takes its name from two prominent Toronto families. T
 he Taylor family was associated with the Don Valley Brick Works\, now home
  to Evergreen Brick Works.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Gro
 up – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\
 n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about **two hours** 
 walking along the trail\, taking our time\, chatting\, and getting to know
  one another.\nThis is a **social walk\, not a race.**\n\nThe route has ve
 ry few hills\, making it a comfortable walk for most people with a reasona
 ble level of fitness.\nWe'll finish back where we started.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typi
 cal Toronto fall weather.\nPlease dress appropriately for the conditions a
 nd wear comfortable walking shoes. The trail may be damp or muddy dependin
 g on recent weather.\nBring water and a snack\, and dress in layers if the
  temperature is changing throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Deta
 ils\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station\, by
  Victoria Park Road.\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup 
 Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on tim
 e. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Victoria Park Subway Station\n\
 n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧
  **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allow
 s us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 W
 hat to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n
 🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n🦟 Bug spray if needed\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 
 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who enjoys fall sc
 enery 🍂\n* People looking for an easy trail\n* Anyone who wants to get 
 outside and get moving\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto's hidden gree
 n spaces\n* Anyone looking for a relaxed social outing\n* People who want 
 to meet new people and make friends\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of tim
 e or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometi
 mes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so plea
 se keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew*
 *\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@ho
 tmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n*
 *Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
