SUMMARY:GHOST TOUR - 👻 The Ghosts of University of Toronto 🎃  with D
 inner! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🎃 
 The Ghosts of the University of Toronto 👻\n\n### A 90-Minute Halloween 
 Ghost Walk Through Toronto's Haunted History\n\nL\nooking for something a 
 little different this Halloween season?\n\nJoin us for a **guided ghost wa
 lk through the University of Toronto campus and its eerie surroundings**\,
  exploring some of the stories\, legends\, and strange histories hidden in
  one of Toronto's oldest neighbourhoods.\nThis isn't one of our regular wa
 lks where we're simply following a trail and enjoying the scenery.\n\n**Th
 is is a curated storytelling experience.**\n\nI've researched the location
 s\, developed the route\, and put together the stories specifically for th
 is experience. We'll explore some of the darker corners of the university 
 and surrounding neighbourhoods while uncovering the people\, places\, and 
 legends that have given them their haunted reputations.\n\n🕯️ Along t
 he way\, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* What the Christies — yes\, *Mr. 
 Christie Cookies* — were hiding in their mansion 🍪\n* The restless li
 ttle girl who is never happy 👧\n* What might really be lurking inside Q
 ueen's Park 👀\n* Haunted stories connected to University of Toronto bui
 ldings\n* The Royal Conservatory of Music\n* The Royal Ontario Museum\n* A
 nd some other stories that are better experienced after dark... 👻\n\nYo
 u don't have to believe in ghosts.\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n
 \n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://
 chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll D
 o\n\nWe'll spend approximately **90 minutes walking through the University
  of Toronto campus and surrounding streets**\, stopping at locations conne
 cted to Toronto's haunted history.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hear stori
 es about some of Toronto's most intriguing characters and locations\n* Exp
 lore the darker history of the University of Toronto\n* Visit locations as
 sociated with ghost stories and local legends\n* Learn the history behind 
 some of the buildings around us\n* Walk through Queen's Park and the surro
 unding area\n* Finish at the **Royal Ontario Museum**\n\nWe'll remain **ou
 tside the buildings** throughout the experience.\nThe walking pace will be
  moderate\, with plenty of stops along the way for stories.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🕯️ This Is More Than a Walk\n\nOur regular walks are about getting ou
 tside\, exploring Toronto\, and meeting people.\nThis one is different.\n\
 n**This is a guided storytelling experience.**\n\nThe route and stories ha
 ve been researched and developed specifically for this event\, so you're n
 ot just following me from one location to another — you're getting a sto
 ry about the city as we go.\nAnd because it's Halloween season\, we'll be 
 doing it after dark. 🎃\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 What to Expect\n\nThis is an o
 utdoor walking experience\, so please dress appropriately for the weather.
 \nWe'll be walking for approximately **90 minutes**\, with regular stops f
 or storytelling.\n\nThere is **no entry into any buildings**\, so you won'
 t need to worry about museum admission or other entrance fees.\nAnd while 
 some of the stories are genuinely creepy\, this isn't designed to be a hor
 ror attraction.\n\nIt's **Toronto history\, local legends\, and storytelli
 ng with a spooky twist.**\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meeti
 ng Location:** In front of the building by the stairs\n🫎 **Look for me 
 in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Start Time:** 7:00 PM sharp\nI will only wait **
 5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Walk
 ing Pace:** Moderate\n🏁 **End Point:** Royal Ontario Museum\n\n***\n\n#
 # 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@h
 otmail.com**\n\nThis is a **curated\, guided storytelling experience**\, r
 ather than one of our regular group walks. The route\, stories\, and histo
 ry have been researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\
 nFood and drinks afterward are optional and are **not included** in the Me
 etup fee.\n\n***\n\n## 🍻 After the Ghost Walk\n\nWe'll finish at the **
 Royal Ontario Museum**.\n\nFor anyone who wants to keep the evening going\
 , we'll walk about 10 minutes over to the **Duke of York** for food\, drin
 ks\, and conversation.\n\nYou don't have to come — but everyone is welco
 me.\nBecause sometimes the best part of a ghost story is having someone to
  talk about it with afterward. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\n
 This is great for:\n\n* Anyone who loves ghost stories 👻\n* History buf
 fs\n* People curious about Toronto's darker side\n* Fans of Halloween\n* A
 nyone who enjoys storytelling\n* People looking for something different to
  do in the city\n* Anyone who wants to meet new people while exploring Tor
 onto\n\nYou don't need to believe in ghosts.\n**Just bring your curiosity.
 **\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if y
 ou're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may 
 need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page 
 for updates.\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event w
 all or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for 
 the ghosts. 👻**\n**Stay for the stories.**\n**Leave with a new connecti
 on — and maybe a new friend.** 🖤
