SUMMARY:🍁 The Fall Colours of Brickworks (Thanksgiving Walk) 🍂
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n🍁 **
 The Fall Colours of Brickworks (Thanksgiving Walk)** 🍂\n\nCelebrate Tha
 nksgiving with a scenic fall walk through Toronto’s ravines as we make o
 ur way to **Evergreen Brick Works**. Along the way\, enjoy the crisp autum
 n air\, brilliant fall colours\, and a peaceful escape from the city.\n\nW
 e’ll spend about **30 minutes exploring the Brick Works**\, taking in it
 s history\, trails\, and unique setting before heading back through **Moun
 t Pleasant Cemetery** — one of Toronto’s largest and oldest cemeteries
 \, with plenty of history and beautiful seasonal scenery.\nFor those who
 ’d like to keep the day going\, we’ll finish with a cozy **Thanksgivin
 g lunch at Swiss Chalet**.\n\nTheir seasonal special is expected to be aro
 und **$18.29 plus tax and tip** and includes stuffing\, cranberry sauce\, 
 your choice of side\, a roll\, and a slice of pie — a pretty good way to
  finish a Thanksgiving walk! 🦃🥧\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **W
 hatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYAN
 rKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n### Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** I will 
 be standing outside of ST. CLAIR SUBWAT STATION right beside the McDonald 
 wearing my Moose Hat. 🦌\n🕛 **Meetup Time:** 12:00pm\n**I will only w
 ait 5 minutes.**\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to 
 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n📍 **
 Ending Spot:** Swiss Chalet\, a few blocks from the station.\n\nPlanning t
 o join us for lunch? Please let me know so I can give Swiss Chalet a rough
  estimate of how many people to expect. They don’t take reservations\, b
 ut I’d like to give them an approximate number so they can be prepared f
 or our group.\n\n🍁 **Please note:** Swiss Chalet is a continuation of t
 his event\, not a separate event for anyone joining us for the walk. If yo
 u are attending the Brick Works walk **and** joining us for lunch at Swiss
  Chalet\, you only pay the **$5 Meetup fee once**.\nIf you are **only join
 ing us at Swiss Chalet** and are not attending the walk\, please sign up f
 or the separate Swiss Chalet event. The **$5 Meetup fee applies** to that 
 event.\n\n***\n\n### What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Good walking shoes 👟\n
 * A jacket or extra layer — fall weather can change quickly\n* Your came
 ra or phone if you want to capture the colours! 📸\n\n***\n\n### More Ab
 out the Brick Works 🧱\n\nFrom 1889 through the 1980s\, the Don Valley B
 rick Works was one of Canada’s leading brickyards. In the 1990s\, the fo
 rmer quarry was restored by the City of Toronto and the Toronto and Region
  Conservation Authority\, transforming the site into the natural and cultu
 ral destination we know today.\nOpened to the public in 1996\, Evergreen B
 rick Works now combines history\, nature\, wildlife\, and trails in the he
 art of Toronto’s ravine system. In autumn\, the surrounding landscape co
 mes alive with reds\, oranges\, and golds\, making it one of the city's gr
 eat places to enjoy the fall colours.\n\n***\n\n✨ **Not sure yet? You ca
 n just show up on the day!**\n⚠️ **Sometimes things happen and I may n
 eed to cancel. Please watch for updates before heading out.**\n\n👤 **Or
 ganized by Mathew.**\nFor questions\, post on the Meetup wall or email **[
 torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmai
 l.com)**
