SUMMARY:👻 Ghost Tour of Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 👻 
 Ghost Tour: Queen West & Yonge Street 🌙\n\n### Restless Spirits\, Stran
 ge Stories & Toronto After Dark\n\nThe thing about ghosts is… **they don
 ’t always stay where they died.**\nSometimes they linger in places they 
 loved. Sometimes they remain where unfinished business keeps them tethered
 . And sometimes\, apparently\, they just really like a particular chair.\n
 \nOn this walking tour\, we'll explore some of the stranger stories connec
 ted to **Queen West and Yonge Street** — from hospitals and theatres to 
 music halls\, historic buildings\, and some rather unexpected places.\nSom
 e of these people met their fate on these streets.\n**Most didn't.**\n\nGh
 osts are funny that way.\n\nThis is a **curated storytelling experience**\
 , combining Toronto history\, local legends\, and some of the city's more 
 unusual ghost stories.\nAnd don't worry — we're not going inside the bui
 ldings.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE]
 (https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 Wha
 t We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the P
 erforming Arts** and make our way east toward Yonge Street.\nAlong the way
 \, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🔫 **Don't play with guns… again**\n
 * 🙏 **“This is my hospital\,” said the Nun**\n* 🎶 **The spirit w
 ho stayed for the music**\n* 🪑 **Who sat in that chair?**\n* 👻 Other
  strange stories\, unexplained encounters\, and Toronto legends\n\nWe'll f
 inish at **Yonge-Dundas Square**.\nThe walk will take approximately **90 m
 inutes**\, depending on the pace of the group.\n\nWe'll remain outdoors th
 roughout the experience and will **not be entering any buildings**.\n\n***
 \n\n## 🌙 A Little About the Experience\n\nThis isn't simply a walk wher
 e someone points out a few supposedly haunted buildings.\nI've researched 
 the stories\, developed the route\, and brought the different pieces toget
 her into a single experience.\nSome stories are rooted in Toronto history.
 \nSome have been passed down as local legends.\nAnd some leave you wonderi
 ng whether there might actually be something to them.\n**You can decide wh
 at you believe.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup L
 ocation:** Outside the **Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts**\n
 🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM shar
 p**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.
 **\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Yon
 ge-Dundas Square**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person
  or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated 
 ghost-walking experience**\, rather than one of our regular social walks. 
 The route\, stories\, and history have been researched and brought togethe
 r specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and wo
 rk that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\
 n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 W
 ater\n📱 Your phone for photos — if you're brave enough. 👻\n\n***\n
 \n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 Peop
 le who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto's strang
 e history\n* 🎭 Theatre and music lovers\n* 🕯️ People who enjoy loc
 al legends and unexplained stories\n* 🚶 People looking for something di
 fferent to do in the evening\n* 😂 Anyone who likes being a little scare
 d without taking it too seriously\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\
 nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welco
 me to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about
  your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancell
 ed or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n
 👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\
 n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the ghosts.**\
 n**Stay for the stories.**\n**Leave wondering what you just heard.** 👻
 🌙
