SUMMARY:🚐 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!  Saturday\, October
  17
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n**🚐 
 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!**\n**Saturday\, October 17**\n\n
 Let’s hit the road for another Doors Open adventure! We’ll be heading 
 to beautiful **Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake** to explore historic buildi
 ngs\, cultural sites\, and hidden spaces that are rarely open to the publi
 c.\nNick has been a **Doors Open Toronto volunteer for over two decades**\
 , and he always enjoys checking out Doors Open events in other cities. Nia
 gara-on-the-Lake is known for its incredible heritage architecture\, charm
 ing streets\, and fascinating history—making it a perfect destination fo
 r a Doors Open day trip.\n\n***\n\n### 🏛️ What is Doors Open?\n\nIf y
 ou’ve never attended before\, **Doors Open** is a free architectural and
  cultural event held in communities across Ontario. For one special weeken
 d\, cities open the doors to historic buildings\, cultural institutions\, 
 churches\, theatres\, and other interesting spaces—many of which are nor
 mally closed to the public.\nVisitors can explore at their own pace\, lear
 n about local history\, and sometimes go behind the scenes with guided tou
 rs or special access.\n\nLearn more about the event here:\n👉 [https://w
 ww.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake](https://www.do
 orsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake)\n\n***\n\n### 🗓
 ️ The Plan\n\n* **Departure:** 8:00 AM from just outside **Christie Stat
 ion**\n* **Transportation:** Rental minivan or SUV\n* **Destination:** **N
 iagara-on-the-Lake**\n* Spend the day exploring **Doors Open sites around 
 town**\n* Time permitting we may be able to visit Niagara Falls after for 
 a few photos/sightseeing\n* **Return to Toronto:** Around **6:00 PM**\, de
 pending on traffic\n\nYou’re welcome to explore with the group or wander
  off to check out sites that interest you most. The day will be relaxed an
 d flexible.\n\n***\n\n### 🍽️ Food & Drink\n\nYou are responsible for 
 **your own food and drink purchases** throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n### 
 💰 Cost\n\n**$60 round-trip**\nThis covers:\n\n* Car rental\n* Insurance
 \n* Fuel\n\nTo secure your spot\, **all participants must e-transfer $60 t
 o:**\n📧 **[nicolasbello@yahoo.com](mailto:nicolasbello@yahoo.com)**\nSp
 ots are limited based on vehicle capacity\, so please RSVP only if you’r
 e able to commit.\n\n***\n\n### 🌦️ Weather Note\n\nThis event **runs 
 rain or shine**\, so please **dress appropriately for the weather**. The g
 ood news is that we’ll be **inside most of the time**\, but there will s
 till be some walking between locations.\n\n***\n\n### 🎒 What to Bring\n
 \n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Curiosity & good vibes\n* A little patien
 ce for traffic (it’s part of the road-trip charm!)\n\nJoin us for a fun 
 architectural adventure and a chance to explore one of Ontario’s most hi
 storic towns. 🚐🏛️
